  "findings": "Inspected the photographed low angular twigs and small oval leaves, explicitly excluding the summer berries and surrounding heather from the spring model. Reduced the original overly dense pilot to fewer stools, twigs and 25 mm leaf envelopes, then inspected all three current sizes and 36 variants. The open low shrub silhouettes span 0.23-0.47 m and retain green branch-following foliage. Individual small flowers and leaf teeth are unresolved at 25 mm; no fruit is generated. Accepted as a stylized spring bilberry ground layer, pending user endorsement.",
